<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.2"
          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
          xml:id="ndm_estimatedrift">

  <info>
    <productname>neurosuite-3</productname>
    <authorgroup>
      <author><personname><firstname>neurosuite-3</firstname>
        <surname>contributors</surname></personname></author>
    </authorgroup>
    <copyright><year>2025</year><holder>neurosuite-3 contributors</holder></copyright>
    <legalnotice><para>GPL-3.0-or-later</para></legalnotice>
  </info>

  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>ndm_estimatedrift</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
  </refmeta>

  <refnamediv>
    <refname>ndm_estimatedrift</refname>
    <refpurpose>
      Estimate in-vivo spatial drift from curated spike-sorting results
    </refpurpose>
  </refnamediv>

  <refsynopsisdiv>
    <cmdsynopsis>
      <command>ndm_estimatedrift</command>
      <arg choice="opt"><replaceable>session</replaceable></arg>
    </cmdsynopsis>
  </refsynopsisdiv>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Description</title>
    <para>
      <command>ndm_estimatedrift</command> reads the curated
      <filename>.clu.N</filename> cluster assignment files and the
      corresponding spike-time <filename>.res.N</filename> and waveform
      <filename>.spk.N</filename> (or <filename>.spkD.N</filename>) files
      for each spikeDetection group, then estimates the in-vivo vertical
      displacement (drift) of each electrode shank over successive time
      windows.
    </para>
    <para>
      Two complementary methods are run and reported per window.  The
      primary method is per-unit spatial-profile cross-correlation: for
      each well-isolated unit the amplitude-vs-depth fingerprint
      (mean PTP per site) is built in a reference window and in every
      subsequent window, and the two profiles are cross-correlated along
      the depth axis with parabolic-fit sub-site refinement.  The shank
      drift is the weighted median of the per-unit shifts (weights =
      sqrt(n_spikes_ref × n_spikes_win)).  A geometric consistency check
      flags units whose pairwise depth distances change by more than
      <parameter>outlierThreshold</parameter> µm and excludes them.
    </para>
    <para>
      The fallback method is population-level amplitude-profile
      cross-correlation: a single mean-PTP-per-site profile is built
      across all non-noise spikes and cross-correlated against the
      reference profile.  This is reported alongside the per-unit
      estimate and is used as the primary value when fewer than
      <parameter>minUnits</parameter> units are tracked.
    </para>
    <para>
      Electrode site geometry is read from inline
      <literal>sitePositions_um</literal> on the spike-detection group
      when present, falling back to the <filename>.probe</filename>
      configuration declared in the session YAML under
      <literal>probes</literal>.  When neither is available a uniform
      50 µm linear spacing is assumed.
    </para>
    <para>
      The result is written to <filename>SESSION.drift</filename> in YAML
      format.  This file is consumed by drift-correction tools (e.g.
      <command>ndm_applydrift</command>) and can be inspected in any
      text editor.  When <filename>SESSION.dat</filename> is present, a
      per-probe binary signal <filename>SESSION.dat.drift.N</filename> is
      also written (int16 µm, one sample per recording sample,
      piecewise-linear interpolation between window midpoints).
    </para>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Prerequisites</title>
    <itemizedlist>
      <listitem><para>
        Spike sorting must be complete:
        <filename>.fet.N</filename>, <filename>.clu.N</filename>,
        <filename>.res.N</filename>, <filename>.spk.N</filename> files must
        exist for all groups.
      </para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>
        Clusters should have been manually curated in
        <application>Klusters</application>.  Cluster 0 (noise) and cluster 1
        (MUA) are excluded by default.
      </para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>
        Python 3 with <package>pyyaml</package> and <package>numpy</package>
        must be installed.
      </para></listitem>
    </itemizedlist>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Parameters</title>
    <para>
      All parameters are optional.  Default values are shown in parentheses.
      Parameters are passed via the ndManager <guilabel>Parameters</guilabel>
      tab or appended to the script invocation.
    </para>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><parameter>windowSec</parameter></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Length of each analysis time window in seconds (default:
          <literal>60</literal>).  Shorter windows yield finer temporal
          resolution but require more spikes per unit per window.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><parameter>minUnits</parameter></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Minimum number of well-isolated units per shank required to compute
          drift for that shank (default: <literal>3</literal>).  Shanks with
          fewer good units in a given window are skipped.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><parameter>minSpikes</parameter></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Minimum number of spikes a unit must fire within a window to be
          included in the CoM computation for that window (default:
          <literal>20</literal>).
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><parameter>excludeNoise</parameter></term>
        <listitem><para>
          If <literal>true</literal> (default), excludes cluster 0 (noise/
          artifact) and cluster 1 (multi-unit activity) from the CoM
          calculation.  Set to <literal>false</literal> to include MUA in the
          estimate, which can help when few well-isolated units are present.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><parameter>outlierThreshold</parameter></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Maximum allowed change (µm) in pairwise depth distance between
          a unit and the others, between the reference and the current
          window, before that unit is flagged as an outlier and excluded
          from the per-unit drift estimate (default:
          <literal>5.0</literal>).  Outliers are still listed in the
          per-window detail block for inspection.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><parameter>probeLibrary</parameter></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Override the probe library search path.  When not set, the plugin
          searches in order: <envar>NEUROSUITE_PROBE_PATH</envar>,
          <filename>~/.local/share/neurosuite/probes/</filename>,
          <filename>/usr/share/neurosuite/probes/</filename>, and
          <filename>probes/</filename> relative to the session directory.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Output File Format</title>
    <para>
      The drift file <filename>SESSION.drift</filename> is a YAML document
      with the following structure:
    </para>
    <programlisting language="yaml"><![CDATA[
drift:
  format: '1.0'
  methods: [per_unit_xcorr, xcorr_population]
  primaryMethod: per_unit_xcorr
  windowSec: 60.0
  minUnits: 3
  minSpikes: 20
  outlierThreshold: 5.0
  probes:
    - probeId: 0
      label: "left CA1"
      shanks:
        - shankIndex: 0
          spikeGroup: 1
          nUnitsQualified: 7
          nUnitsInRef: 6
          refWindowIndex: 0
          refWindowT_start: 0.0
          maxAbsDrift_um: 8.42
          driftRate_um_per_hr: 3.1
          windows:
            - t_start: 0.0
              t_end: 60.0
              drift_um: 0.0
              per_unit_xcorr:
                drift_um: 0.0
                n_inlier_units: 6
                units:
                  - { unit: 2, ref_com_um: 245.3, win_com_um: 245.3,
                      xcorr_shift_um: 0.0, com_delta_um: 0.0,
                      weight: 142.0, outlier: false }
              xcorr_population:
                drift_um: 0.0
            - t_start: 60.0
              t_end: 120.0
              drift_um: -1.83
              per_unit_xcorr:
                drift_um: -1.85
                n_inlier_units: 7
                units: [...]
              xcorr_population:
                drift_um: -1.78
    ]]></programlisting>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><structfield>drift_um</structfield></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Combined per-window estimate, signed displacement in
          micrometres relative to the reference window.  Positive =
          probe moved deeper into tissue; negative = retraction.
          A weighted blend of per-unit xcorr and population xcorr when
          enough inlier units are tracked; falls back to either method
          alone otherwise.  <literal>null</literal> when neither
          method produced an estimate for the window.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><structfield>per_unit_xcorr.drift_um</structfield></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Weighted median of per-unit cross-correlation shifts (µm).
          Sub-site precision via parabolic interpolation around the
          correlation peak.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><structfield>xcorr_population.drift_um</structfield></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Population-level cross-correlation shift (µm) using the
          mean-PTP-per-site amplitude profile across all non-noise
          spikes in the window.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><structfield>units</structfield></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Per-unit detail for the window: cluster id, reference and
          window CoM, xcorr shift, CoM delta (cross-check), weight, and
          outlier flag.  Units flagged as outliers contribute zero
          weight to the rigid-body estimate but remain visible for
          inspection.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Session YAML Requirements</title>
    <para>
      For drift estimation to use accurate probe geometry the session YAML
      should include a <literal>probes</literal> section and
      <literal>probeId</literal> / <literal>shankIndex</literal> fields on
      each anatomical group entry:
    </para>
    <programlisting language="yaml"><![CDATA[
probes:
  - id: 0
    probeFile: neuronexus/Buzsaki64.probe
    label: "left CA1"
    channelOffset: 0
    anatomicalGroups: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]

anatomicalDescription:
  channelGroups:
    - id: 1
      probeId: 0
      shankIndex: 0
      channels:
        - { id: 0, skip: 0 }
        ...
    ]]></programlisting>
    <para>
      Without these fields a uniform 50 µm linear spacing is assumed and
      <structfield>probeId</structfield> defaults to 0 for all groups.
    </para>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Files</title>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><filename>SESSION.yaml</filename> (or .xml)</term>
        <listitem><para>Session parameter file (mandatory input).</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><filename>SESSION.res.N</filename></term>
        <listitem><para>Spike timestamps for group N (mandatory input).</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><filename>SESSION.clu.N</filename></term>
        <listitem><para>Curated cluster labels for group N (mandatory input).</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><filename>SESSION.spk.N</filename> /
              <filename>SESSION.spkD.N</filename></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Spike waveforms for group N (optional; used for accurate CoM
          and amplitude profiles).  When both are present
          <filename>.spkD.N</filename> (stderiv pipeline) is preferred —
          its on-disk layout matches <filename>.spk.N</filename> (int16
          sample-major, full nCG channels).  When neither is present
          spike counts are used as an amplitude proxy.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><filename>SESSION.drift</filename></term>
        <listitem><para>Output drift file (YAML).</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><filename>SESSION.dat.drift.N</filename></term>
        <listitem><para>
          Optional binary side-output, one file per probe (1-based
          index N matching the YAML <literal>probes</literal> list
          order).  Contains <literal>n_total_samples</literal> int16
          values (µm), one per recording sample, generated by
          piecewise-linear interpolation of the per-window drift
          estimates.  Written only when <filename>SESSION.dat</filename>
          is present.
        </para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>See Also</title>
    <para>
      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>ndm_applydrift</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
